course: dictionary
lesson: 7924
title: Reactive: quick to respond
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reactive is an adjective. It describes something that changes when something else touches it or happens to it. In science, a reactive substance changes quickly when it meets another substance. «Oxygen is a very reactive gas» means oxygen changes other things quickly when they touch it.
explain: The sentence gives you a clue: «a cut apple and a cut piece of some metals both change colour in air, in very different ways.» Both things change when they meet air, so reactive means ready to change when it meets something else. Ask yourself: what changes, and what is it touching?
explain: In everyday life, reactive means acting only after something has happened, instead of planning ahead. A reactive team waits for problems and then fixes them. The opposite is proactive, which means stopping problems before they start. Reactive can also mean easily upset, like a reactive dog that barks at everything.
explain: Reactive has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is right. Science words usually mention substances or metals. Everyday words usually mention people, teams or behaviour.
fact: Reactive means likely to change quickly when it meets another substance.
fact: «Oxygen» is a very reactive gas.
fact: In the reactivity series, potassium and sodium are the most reactive metals.
fact: Gold is not reactive, which is why it stays shiny.
fact: A reactive person acts after problems happen; a proactive person prevents them.
exercise: «Oxygen is a very reactive gas.» What does reactive mean here? | *Likely to change quickly when it meets another substance | Only used in cooking | Full of colour | Very heavy and slow to move
exercise: Gold stays shiny because it is not reactive. What does this tell you about gold? | *Gold does not change easily when it meets other things | Gold is always wet | Gold is very loud | Gold is soft and bendy
exercise: A team that only fixes problems after they happen is what kind of team? | Proactive | Cheerful | Silent | *Reactive
test: Which word means the opposite of reactive in everyday life, meaning a person who prevents problems before they start? | Reactive | Gloomy | *Proactive | Ancient
test: Which word describes a dog that barks at everything, as it is easily upset? | *Reactive | Luminous | Curt | Barely
exam: The reactive dog barked at every passing car. What does reactive suggest about the dog? | *Easily upset and quick to respond strongly | Planning ahead to stop trouble | Calm and sleepy | Shiny like gold
